#message 5 "\"Case details are on the board, Reyes. Kit's on the shelf, forms are in the IN tray, and Bukowski is out front with the car. Check the driver's story before you believe it.\""
#message 6 "Sergeant Prakash has thirty years on the force and a gray mustache that has outlasted four police chiefs. He is moving a form from one tray to another."
#message 7 "CASE 114. Break-in, Hollis Pharmacy, 12 Main Street. Reported 2:10 AM by Gus Tully, driver, Swiftline Deliveries, van 7. Pharmacist: Ada Hollis. Swiftline delivery logs are kept in the Records Office."
#message 8 "The front desk is worn oak. On it sit a dispatch radio, a nameplate reading SGT. R. PRAKASH, and three wire trays."
#message 9 "Three wire trays, labeled IN, OUT and WRONG TRAY. The WRONG TRAY is the fullest. The IN tray holds blank report forms."
#message 10 "You take a blank report form from the IN tray.\n\n\"That's the IN tray, Reyes. Good. When it's filled out, it goes in the OUT tray. Not the other one.\""
#message 11 "You already have a report form. One is plenty."
#message 12 "You take the evidence kit from the shelf: a camera, evidence bags and gloves."
#message 13 "\"That kit is for officers with an assignment, Reyes. Talk to me first.\""
#message 14 "You already have the evidence kit."
#message 15 "The equipment shelf holds an evidence kit: camera, evidence bags and gloves."
#message 16 "The equipment shelf is empty."
#message 17 "\"Reyes!\" Prakash calls. \"Assignment first. Then the street.\""
#message 18 "\"Dispatch. No assignment on file for you yet, Reyes. The sergeant is standing right there.\""
#message 19 "\"Dispatch. Case 114, break-in at Hollis Pharmacy, 12 Main Street. Reporting party Gus Tully, Swiftline van 7, 2:10 AM. Bukowski is out front with the car. I'll be here.\""
#message 20 "Millhaven Police, badge 2217. Still shiny."
#message 21 "Your shoulder radio. Dispatch is one call away."
#message 22 "Prakash glances at your badge. \"I issued you that on Monday, Reyes. I remember.\""
#message 23 "You need the camera from the evidence kit."
#message 24 "Save the film for the crime scene."
#message 25 "The Records Office door. Behind it: delivery logs, old case files and a clerk who guards both."
#message 26 "The glass doors open onto Main Street. The patrol car is parked just outside."
#message 27 "Bukowski is waiting with the patrol car out front."
#message 28 "You need a report form first. The IN tray has plenty."
#message 29 "\"A report needs a case, Reyes. Evidence, a suspect, an arrest. Go get them.\""
#message 30 "Gus Tully is out on Main Street. Check his story there."
#message 31 "Step up to the desk first."
#message 32 "Green fluorescent tubes hum overhead. Everyone in the lobby looks slightly seasick."
#message 33 "Talk to Sergeant Prakash, read the board, and pick up what you need before heading out the front doors."
#message 34 "That's out in the district, not here in the lobby."
#message 35 "A blank incident report, four pages with carbon copies."
#message 36 "Camera, evidence bags and gloves."
#message 37 "A rubber plant. Someone waters it with cold coffee."
#message 38 "Prakash takes the form, reads the first line and hands it back. \"Blank, Reyes. Reports work better with words in them.\""
#message 39 "Walk to a door to leave: Records on the left, Main Street on the right."
#message 40 "The dispatch radio's red light blinks every few seconds."
